abstractions

	^ 'Core domain:
- HSKCharacter: value object for one Chinese character. Instance variables: traditional, simplified, pinyin, zhuyin, definition, frequency, hasErrorLoading, module, phonems, wordsAmount, radicals, graphicals, hfwords, mdwords. Collections are lazily created (pinyin, definition, phonems, radicals, graphicals, hfwords, mdwords answer a Set). Defaults: frequency 4000, wordsAmount 0. Equality (= and hash) uses traditional plus definition; < compares traditional; asCharacter answers traditional; asHSKString wraps it in HSKString; asUnicode delegates to traditional asUnicode. isRoot is true when radicals includes self; isHolder is false; isHSKString is false (HSKString does not implement it). mark: stores a module symbol, module answers HSKModule module: symbol, setupModule normalizes a non-String module to its name. Phonetics: phoneticDistance: scores pinyin pairs (same length +1, left and right alignment matches +1, mismatches -1, spaces 0); pronouncedLike: accepts same species and equal, shared pinyin, or equal zhuyin; phoneticFamily ranks all characters by distance but sends HSKCharacter instances, which is not defined. Radicals: distanceToRadical is 0 for a root, 1 when a radical is a root, else 2; radicalDistanceTo: builds a ByteArray and is unfinished; potentialPhonems returns radicals. hasErrorLoading sets the flag to true; hasError reads it.
- HSKCharacterHolder: placeholder for characters missing from the corpus. traditional and simplified answer the single char; definition answers {char}; radicals answers {}; pinyin answers a Set; module answers HSKModule nohsk; isHolder is true; hasError is false; traditional: and simplified: are no-ops. It now also answers neutral corpus selectors: hfwords, mdwords, graphicals and phonems are empty Sets, frequency is 4000, wordsAmount 0, zhuyin nil, asCharacter/asUnicode answer the char, < by char, = and hash by char, so it is safe for provider select:/detect: over a polluted corpus.
- HSKString: ArrayedCollection of HSKCharacter or HSKCharacterHolder. fromString: and fromString:provider: map each Character through the provider detectOrCreateHolder:. simplifiedString and traditionalString join the parts; pinyin asserts size 1; definition consults the dictionary trie and prepends the single character definition (all collections normalized with asArray before joining); module answers the maximum module; printString answers traditionalString; asHSKString answers self.
- HSKModule: interned value object (name and order) kept in a class-side Dictionary. Class methods hsk1..hsk6 (orders 1..6), nohsk (50), dictionary (7), latinLetter (0). module: validates against a whitelist and performs the matching class method. Comparisons use order (<, >, <=, max:). printOn: writes Module (<name>). Whitelisted names number, punctuation and hskPunctuation have no class methods.
- HSKCharacterProvider: singleton corpus. default builds one and sets hskCharacters from decodeHskCharacters (STONReader over the embedded base64 literal encodedInstances). detect:, detect:ifNone:, select:, detectOrCreateHolder: (search by simplified or traditional, otherwise create and add an HSKCharacterHolder), hskCharacters:, encodeInstancesInto: (STON, UTF-8, base64 file). basicCharacters, children: and strictChildren: read the instances variable, which default never sets.
- HSKCharacterMarker: stateless helper; mark: assigns #hsk1..#hsk6 or #nohsk to a character using embedded character lists.
- CharsetCategory: Unicode block interval plus category name. Embeds Blocks-12.0.0.txt; unicode parses it lazily; latin1 is broken (undeclared Latin1 global); categoryFor:, allCharacters, isBasicLatin, isLatin1, isLatin1Supplement.

Application layer (on top of the SRS domain):
- HSKApp: session model. users collection of SRSUser, currentUser, style symbol (#simplified default), own Announcer. newUser creates SRSUser, ensures the dictionary is seeded, runs user xiaoWangZi (goal built over the embedded corpus story), registers and announces HSKUserAdded + HSKUserSelected. currentUser: validates membership and announces HSKUserSelected. style: announces HSKStyleChanged. isTraditional/isSimplified predicates.
- HSKKnowledgeOverview: read model of one HSKApp. entries (goal unlockedContent), totalAmount/unlockedAmount/lockedAmount, levelOf:/nextReviewOf:, spellingOf: anEntry (HSKString traditionalString or simplifiedString following the app style).
- HSKReminderPage: exercise page model around SRSPhoneticExercise over the current goal. current (HSKPhoneticTest), currentSubject, currentSpelling, currentMeanings, hintText, hasNext, next (counts processed), answer: aPinyin (assertWith flow), giveUp, todoAmount, doneAmount.
- HSKQuizPage: multiple choice phonetic exercise over the goal characters. target plus options (3 distractors chosen by maximal phoneticDistance), targetSpelling and spellingOf: following the app style, answer: aContent compares identity, submits the review on #phonetic and answers a boolean; next never repeats the previous target.
- HSKDesktopShell: ToPane root of the application (Toplo). Header (usersBar with one button per user, newUserButton, styleButton), knowledge pane, ToTabPaneElement exercises with pages Pinyin Reminder and Pinyin Quiz, statusLabel. app: wires the app announcer (refresh on HSKUserAdded/Selected/StyleChanged) and the current user announcer (statusLabel update on SRSLevelUp). knowledgeSpellingOf: and statusText expose state for tests. Class side ensureNSimSunAvailable registers simsun.ttc in AeFontManager and sets it as defaultFace; on: calls it. openOn: opens a Bee themed BlSpace 800x600.'